        "modelingNotes": [
          "Exact S4-J screw-terminal socket for 14-pin C4 relays, selected by WoR 3.2 p.347 and detailed on p.348. Manufacturer retained as Releco per job identity; evidence is ComatReleco.",
          "C.n denotes wire clamp n; M.n denotes the matching socket mating contact n. C/M are model aliases, not manufacturer markings. Figure 2 shows both numbered interfaces from the socket insertion side; no underside mirror, coordinates or installed wiring is inferred.",
          "Figure 1 maps physical numbers to relay-function labels: 1=12, 2=14, 3=11, 4=22, 5=24, 6=21, 7=32, 8=34, 9=31, 10=42, 11=44, 12=41, 13=A1, 14=A2. Figure 2 instead prints 14|21 at clamp 14, conflicting with figure 1. Physical number 14 is unambiguous; A2 is recorded only as figure 1's functional label.",
          "Fourteen independent passive socket conductors connect C.n to M.n, n=1 through 14, as identified by matching socket-contact and clamp numbers in figure 2. Represent these factory paths using explicit project jumpers listed in conformance.fixedLinks. Singleton bus functions and connector metadata do not establish continuity.",
          "Figure 1 shows the compatible relay coil and changeover functions, not components fitted inside the bare socket. Do not connect different numbered paths permanently, add coil behavior, assert contact normal state or fit suppression/indicator circuitry. All connections are application-dependent; none is universally required.",
          "Manufacturer rated load is 10 A / 250 V. Capability is recorded here rather than nominal_voltage; no assigned voltage or AC-only classification is inferred. Dielectric strength is 2.5 kV rms for one minute, terminals-to-DIN-rail and terminal-to-terminal. This does not establish a conductive rail bond.",
          "Single-wire capacity 1.5 mm2 or 2 x 1.5 mm2; uncrimped multi-wire 0.34–1 mm2. M3.5 combination screws, nominal torque 0.8 Nm. Operating temperature -40 to +60 degrees C; storage -40 to +80 degrees C, no ice. PA/PC housing; TH35 or back-panel mounting. Shared connection policy accommodates a factory-path representation plus external wiring; it is not a general multiple-conductor approval.",
          "The optional plastic retaining clip S3-CM/CP-15B is mechanical and contributes no modeled terminals. No PE, shield, communication, auxiliary electrical connector or rail bonding terminal is documented. Complete coverage is for the catalog bare socket's 14 paths, not an installed relay/accessory assembly."
        ]
      },
      "connectionCoverage": {
        "status": "complete",
        "notes": "Fourteen wire clamps and fourteen corresponding socket mating contacts, physical numbers 1–14, comprise fourteen separate factory paths. C/M distinguish modeled interfaces. No fitted relay, electrical accessory or rail bond is asserted. Figure 2's clamp-14 sublabel conflicts with figure 1; physical number 14 is retained."
      },
